    "helpClose": "Close",
    "helpBody": "<h3>Start with your photos</h3>\n<p>Use <b>Add images</b> or drag photos into the sidebar. In the desktop app, <b>Choose folder</b> opens the system folder picker. Local browser use also offers <b>Import path</b>; the hosted website cannot read a path on your computer. Importing does not start recognition.</p>\n<p><b>Ultra</b> combines the algorithm with SAM. <b>Lite</b> is faster and uses less memory. <b>Custom</b> lets you adjust the algorithm yourself. Click ⓘ for details.</p>\n<h3>Recognize photos</h3>\n<p>In Ultra and Lite, <b>Recognize all</b> processes only unrecognized photos and keeps existing results. Keep the page open. <b>Stop after this image</b> finishes processing the current image, then stops the batch.</p>\n<p><b>Recognize current</b> works on the selected photo. Ultra saves a new result directly; for an existing result, it shows a preview. Choose <b>Adopt result</b> to replace the marks, or <b>Cancel preview</b> to keep the existing marks. Lite recounts directly. It asks for confirmation if the photo has manual changes, notes or verification history.</p>\n<h3>Adjust and recount</h3>\n<p>Drag a slider or type a number. Bright green in <b>Live foreground preview</b> shows selected pixels, not counted colonies. <b>Apply</b> saves your settings for this page session and closes the panel; it does not run recognition. <b>Adjust</b> opens it again. Unapplied changes are not used.</p>\n<p>Custom uses the adjustable algorithm, without SAM. Its <b>Recognize all</b> also recounts machine-only results. It skips manual edits, notes, adjusted boundaries, manual mode and any verification history, including withdrawn records. Photos you have only viewed are still recounted. For a photo in <b>Pure manual</b> mode, first choose <b>More → Mode → Automatic + manual</b>. Then use <b>Recognize current</b> and confirm to recount a skipped photo.</p>\n<h3>Check and edit</h3>\n<p>Rose circles are machine marks; blue circles are manual marks. They indicate centers, not exact outlines. Click to add, right-click to remove, or drag a box quickly to remove several. Hold and drag to pan; scroll to zoom; press <b>F</b> to fit. <b>← / →</b> switches photos unless an input, slider or selector has focus. <b>Cmd/Ctrl Z</b> undoes edits. The <b>Manual marks</b> control sets the size of new marks. For the counting area, use <b>More → Adjust medium boundary</b>.</p>\n<h3>Status and deletion</h3>\n<p>Hollow dot: unrecognized. Light gray: machine result. Dark gray: viewed or edited. A dark dot does not mean the result has been verified. <b>Batch delete</b> enables selection; <b>Select all</b> toggles all/none. <b>Delete selected</b> removes session photos and records after confirmation. It cannot be undone; original files stay unchanged.</p>\n<h3>Save your results</h3>\n<p>Notes save automatically. <b>Export</b> offers CSV counts or a ZIP with annotated photos and state files. The desktop app opens a system save dialog; a browser uses its download settings.</p>\n<p>Export before closing. Normal local startup opens an empty session; refreshing keeps the current work. A command-line workspace chosen with <b>--root</b> is retained. The hosted website also uses temporary sessions.</p>\n<section class=\"review-help\"><h3>Verification queues</h3><p>After checking the marks, confirm them under <b>Accuracy verification</b> and click <b>Save colony verification</b>. Viewing does not confirm anything. Later edits can invalidate confirmation. Confirm the medium boundary only after checking it.</p></section>\n<div class=\"help-footer\">\n  <p><b>Authors</b></p>\n  <p>Jianghua Zhang (张江华) &mdash;\n    <a href=\"mailto:zhangjianghua@westlake.edu.cn\">zhangjianghua@westlake.edu.cn</a></p>\n  <p>Xinyu Wang (王欣宇) &mdash;\n    <a href=\"mailto:wangxinyu30@westlake.edu.cn\">wangxinyu30@westlake.edu.cn</a></p>\n  <p>Wenhao Zhou (周文浩) &mdash;\n    <a href=\"mailto:zhouwenhao@westlake.edu.cn\">zhouwenhao@westlake.edu.cn</a></p>\n  <p>Zhanyi Zhu (朱展翼) &mdash;\n    <a href=\"mailto:zhuzhanyi@westlake.edu.cn\">zhuzhanyi@westlake.edu.cn</a></p>\n</div>",
